      "message": "Hi @spinler@us.ibm.com,\n\nThanks again for the review and for looping me in.\n\nI still have one concern from my earlier comment (Patchset 5, Nov 30). In the multi-button case, getHostNumStr() returns \"01\". When we build:\n\n    objPathName \u003d CHASSIS_STATE_OBJECT_NAME + hostNumStr;\n\nthe chassis state object path becomes `/xyz/openbmc_project/state/chassis01`. The chassis state object provided by phosphor-state-manager is `/xyz/openbmc_project/state/chassis1`, so the resulting path is invalid. Because of that, the power control cannot be executed and the FIO power button ends up having no effect.\n\nI’m planning to help address this issue in a follow-up patch, but I wanted to make sure we’re aligned on the problem before this change is merged.\n\n\n\nThanks,\nLiora",
